            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0664" n="614" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv12/pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.011102/198: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Albert Halstead to the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-24T10:30:00+01:00">July 24, 1919—10:30
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 25—2 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>647. Your 137<anchor n="79" xml:id="d240-f1"/> not received when telegram number
                    (apparent omission) [646, July 24, 7 a.m.?] was written. Will inform commission
                    later in day extent to which wholly unofficial negotiations proposed. I have not
                    seen Boehm nor Bauer on the subject but have acted through Cunningham and
                    Commission is in no sense committed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Halstead</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
